---
import TechniquePost from "../../layouts/TechniquePost.astro"
import TextareaBuild from "../../components/UnderTheHood/TextareaBuild.astro"
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components"
---

<TechniquePost slug="textarea-field-sizing">
  <section>
    <h2 id="the-problem">The problem</h2>
    <p>
      A <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> is as tall as its <code>rows</code> attribute
      says, no matter what's in it. Short notes leave empty space, long ones scroll
      inside a tiny box.
    </p>
    <p>
      The usual fix is JavaScript that listens to <code>input</code>, resets the
      height and sets it to <code>scrollHeight</code> on every keystroke. Not anymore.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="the-trick">The trick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>field-sizing: content</code> sizes the textarea to its text: it grows
        as you type and shrinks as you delete
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>lh</code> is one line of the textarea's own text, so limits read as
        line counts
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>min-block-size</code> keeps at least three lines, <code
          >max-block-size</code
        > caps it at 20, then it scrolls
      </li>
      <li><code>resize: block</code> still lets the user drag it taller</li>
    </ul>
    <Code
      lang="css"
      code={`textarea {
  block-size: auto;
  field-sizing: content;
  max-block-size: var(--_max-block-size, 20lh);
  min-block-size: calc(
    var(--padding-block) * 2 + var(--border-width) * 2 + 3lh
  );
  resize: block;
}`}
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>
    <TextareaBuild />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fallback">Fallback</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Browsers without <code>field-sizing</code> ignore it, and the textarea keeps
        its <code>rows</code> height, never less than three lines
      </li>
      <li>Long text scrolls and the resize handle still works</li>
      <li>Nothing breaks, it just doesn't grow</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</TechniquePost>
